{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_webflux_antipattern_project", "label": "webflux-antipattern README", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_multi_tenant_context_propagation", "label": "Multi-tenant context propagation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WebFlux execution hops across threads (subscribeOn, thread pools, event-loop workers), so per-thread state such as ThreadLocal cannot reliably carry request-scoped state like the current tenant through a reactive pipeline."}, {"id": "readme_threadlocal_antipattern", "label": "Antipattern 1: ThreadLocal/InheritableThreadLocal for request-scoped state", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The filter stores the tenant in a ThreadLocal and relies on it still being present, but WebFlux hops threads (subscribeOn, pooled schedulers) and a plain ThreadLocal does not travel with the execution."}, {"id": "readme_stale_pooled_thread_context_antipattern", "label": "Antipattern 2: Stale data from reusing a pooled thread's inherited context", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An InheritableThreadLocal is copied only once, when a worker thread is created; a pooled boundedElastic worker that inherited tenant A keeps serving tenant A's data after the request thread moved to tenant B, returning wrong-tenant data rather than an error."}, {"id": "readme_eager_evaluation_antipattern", "label": "Antipattern 3: Eager evaluation of per-subscription state", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "getUser(long id) reads the tenant context synchronously at call time, before the Mono is built; if the context changes before subscription, the stale already-baked-in tenant is used."}, {"id": "readme_reactor_context", "label": "Reactor Context propagation (contextWrite)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reactor Context travels with the subscription instead of the thread, so request-scoped state survives thread hand-off regardless of which thread executes the work."}, {"id": "readme_lazy_resolution_defer", "label": "Lazy resolution via Mono.defer / Mono.deferContextual", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deferring resolution means the tenant is read at subscription time (per-subscription, not per-call), making it immune to thread hand-off and to context changes between call and subscription."}, {"id": "readme_spring_profile_switching", "label": "Runtime switching via Spring profiles (antipattern / recommended)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same feature is implemented twice, wrong way and recommended way, and selected at runtime by profile; application.yaml defaults spring.profiles.default to antipattern."}, {"id": "readme_tenantidentifierfilter_antipattern", "label": "filter.antipattern.TenantIdentifierFilter", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_tenantidentifierfilter_recommended", "label": "filter.recommended.Tena